# Service Rules for SMS (Skill Management System)

## 1. General

-   Follow Feature-Sliced Design (FSD).
-   Use TypeScript (strict mode). No `any`.
-   Use React function components and hooks.
-   Keep code simple, modular, and maintainable.

## 2. Project Structure (FSD)

The only valid folders:

-   src/app
-   src/widgets
-   src/entities
-   src/features
-   src/shared
-   src/store

Rules:

-   shared → UI, hooks, utils, types, configs.
-   entities → domain models and UI.
-   features → user actions and business logic.
-   widgets → composite UI blocks.
-   app → routing, layouts, providers.

## 3. Path Aliases

Use only:

-   `@/*` → `src/*`
-   `@public/*` → project root.

## 4. Styling

-   Use SCSS Modules only (`*.module.scss`).
-   Use `classnames` for dynamic styles.
-   No inline CSS except minor cases.

## 5. State Management

-   Use Redux Toolkit.
-   Use slices for each domain.
-   Persist only allowed slices (`windows`, `percent`).
-   No non-serializable values in Redux.
-   All async logic must use RTK thunks.

## 6. API & Networking

-   Use Axios instance from `shared/lib/api`.
-   Include interceptors for access/refresh tokens.
-   No raw `fetch()` unless explicitly required.
-   All API responses must be typed.

## 7. Authentication

-   Access token → localStorage.
-   Refresh token → HTTP-only cookies.
-   Token refresh handled automatically in interceptors.

## 8. WebSocket

-   Use `useWebSocket` hook.
-   WS URL must come from environment variables.
-   Implement reconnect and error handling.

## 9. Components

-   One component per folder:
    ComponentName/
    ComponentName.tsx  
     ComponentName.module.scss  
     index.ts

Rules:

-   Props must be strictly typed.
-   No default exports.
-   Use small, focused components.

## 10. Testing

-   Use Jest + Testing Library.
-   Test all features and reusable components.
-   Add mocks for SVG, images, API calls.

## 11. Storybook

-   Every reusable UI component must have a story.
-   Follow CSF3 format.
-   Keep story files minimal and consistent.

## 12. Code Quality

-   Follow ESLint config strictly.
-   No warnings in PRs.
-   Use Prettier for formatting.
-   No commented-out code.
-   No console logs.

## 13. Performance

-   Use React.memo, useCallback, useMemo when necessary.
-   Avoid large rerenders.
-   Apply lazy loading for heavy components.
-   Avoid storing large or complex objects in Redux.

## 14. Security

-   Do not expose sensitive data.
-   Validate all inputs and API responses.
-   Handle all errors gracefully.

## 15. Cursor Agent Specific

-   Follow FSD boundaries strictly.
-   Only create files inside valid layers.
-   Do not restructure architecture unless explicitly asked.
-   Maintain existing coding style and naming.
-   Always use TypeScript types and interfaces.
-   When editing existing files, preserve structure and logic.
-   Return only code when user requests generation.
